> show z + 1
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
_(z: complex) = z + 1
  -> complex
> show w * z
  note: w, z are taken as complex (no x or y here; say w: real for a real variable)
_(w: complex, z: complex) = w*z
  -> complex
> show re(z)
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
_(z: complex) = re(z)
  -> complex
> show im(w + z)
  note: w, z are taken as complex (no x or y here; say w: real for a real variable)
_(w: complex, z: complex) = im(w + z)
  -> complex
> show conj(z) * z
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
_(z: complex) = conj(z)*z
  -> complex
> show z * conj(z)
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
_(z: complex) = z*conj(z)
  -> complex
> show z + x
_(z: real, x: real) = z + x
  -> real
> show abs(z)
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
_(z: complex) = abs(z)
  -> complex
> show re(3 + 4i)
_() = re(4i + 3)
  -> complex
> show im(3 + 4i)
_() = im(4i + 3)
  -> complex
> show abs(3 + 4i)
_() = abs(4i + 3)
  -> complex
> show conj(3 + 4i)
_() = conj(4i + 3)
  -> complex
> show |3 + 4i|
_() = abs(4i + 3)
  -> complex
> show real(3 + 4i)
_() = 4i + 3
  -> complex
> show modulus(3 + 4i)
  note: modulus(...) read as multiplication: modulus is not a function
_(modulus: real) = modulus*(4i + 3)
  -> complex
> show re(z: complex)
_(z: complex) = re(z)
  -> complex
> show im(z: complex)
_(z: complex) = im(z)
  -> complex
> show abs(z: complex)
_(z: complex) = abs(z)
  -> complex
> show arg(z: complex)
_(z: complex) = arg(z)
  -> complex
> show real(z: complex)
_(z: complex) = z
  -> complex
